Visually, "Hot Rod" is instantly recognizable by its dark gunmetal upper torso and vibrant red legs decorated with custom hot-rod flame decals—a direct nod to Tony's beloved '32 Ford Flathead hot rod from the first Iron Man film. It served as the technological precursor to the War Machine Mark II and Iron Patriot suits, testing lightweight reinforced plates that could handle heavy ballistic impacts without requiring the massive bulk of the original Mark I War Machine frame.

In Iron Man 3, Mark XXII drops into the battle at the Norco oil rig during the House Party Protocol, engaging Extremis soldiers on foot before being destroyed alongside the rest of the fleet during the "Clean Slate" protocol.
